WEBVTT

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:10.720
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning all, you alright? Quick one today, Thursday 08 January. Let's get round it.</v>

00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:16.210
<v Jamie Brennan>Morning. Bit rough after the football last night, to be honest. Absolute robbery.</v>

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:19.739
<v Tomasz Nowak>Here we go.</v>

00:00:21.109 --> 00:00:23.910
<v Hannah Price>You say that every time your lot lose.</v>

00:00:24.469 --> 00:00:26.920
<v Jamie Brennan>No, no, genuinely, that ref was shocking.</v>

00:00:28.269 --> 00:00:37.020
<v Sarah Okafor>Save it for break, Jamie. Also, don't forget the charity bake sale on Friday. Bring cash, and no, I'm not accepting 'forgot my wallet' again.</v>

00:00:38.119 --> 00:00:43.020
<v Fiona Doyle>I've already had three emails about brownies, so it's clearly the main production priority.</v>

00:00:44.259 --> 00:00:45.659
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Critical path item, that.</v>

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:48.909
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, actual plant. Any overnight issues?</v>

00:00:49.829 --> 00:01:01.030
<v Hannah Price>Nothing major from quality. I noticed the gas valve on one was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down, so just an observation, not asking for anything on it.</v>

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:12.329
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, noted. Same from me, I heard a slight rattle from the alarm box, nothing to action yet, just keep an ear on it if you're passing.</v>

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:17.209
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Alarm history looked clean when I checked this morning, no weird trips.</v>

00:01:17.689 --> 00:01:25.040
<v Jamie Brennan>And just so it's said, I tested the HRSG yesterday and it's all fine now, so that's done, not for today.</v>

00:01:27.129 --> 00:01:36.930
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. Cheers. Anything still blocked, we've still got the usual one: still waiting on parts for the GT1 Fuel Gas Valve, nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:43.900
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, dead in the water on that till stores actually sees the bits.</v>

00:01:44.709 --> 00:01:47.159
<v Jamie Brennan>Oi, not me this time. Supplier side.</v>

00:01:48.349 --> 00:01:53.250
<v Priya Raman>I signed into the trend packs before this, no fresh alarms off GT1 anyway.</v>

00:01:53.569 --> 00:01:55.670
<v Sarah Okafor>Fine. Hannah, you had line stuff?</v>

00:01:58.129 --> 00:02:04.079
<v Hannah Price>Yeah. I signed off the inspection on the line 2 on Tuesday, so that's closed out already.</v>

00:02:06.049 --> 00:02:08.150
<v Sarah Okafor>Lovely. Keep that one buried then.</v>

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:14.530
<v Fiona Doyle>Schedule-wise today is mostly tidy apart from the Engel work if we can get the paperwork straight.</v>

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:25.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, on that, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Engel by Thursday. I'll pick that up myself so nobody else chase it.</v>

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.120
<v Tomasz Nowak>By Thursday this week, yeah?</v>

00:02:30.659 --> 00:02:32.759
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, by Thursday. I'll own it.</v>

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:36.930
<v Fiona Doyle>I'll mark boss against that then.</v>

00:02:39.030 --> 00:02:49.180
<v Sarah Okafor>Next one, Priya, can you check the guarding on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot next week? I want a proper look, not just a glance walking past.</v>

00:02:50.169 --> 00:02:58.919
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, Priya can do that. I'll check the guarding on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot next week and feed back if anything's out.</v>

00:02:59.490 --> 00:03:01.939
<v Hannah Price>Good shout after the near miss chat.</v>

00:03:04.139 --> 00:03:11.139
<v Sarah Okafor>Which brings me to that, Han, can you write up the near miss at the pick and place on two?</v>

00:03:12.689 --> 00:03:21.439
<v Hannah Price>Yeah, I'll do it. I'll write up the near miss at the pick and place on two today once I've pulled the witness notes together.</v>

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.509
<v Sarah Okafor>Nice one.</v>

00:03:25.810 --> 00:03:38.060
<v Priya Raman>While we're on rotating kit, I'll take vibration readings on the GT2 Number 2 Bearing by the end of the week. I was over there yesterday and I'd rather get a baseline before it drifts.</v>

00:03:39.599 --> 00:03:43.449
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Makes sense. Trend it against the last set if you can.</v>

00:03:44.689 --> 00:03:46.789
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, I'll grab the old numbers.</v>

00:03:48.789 --> 00:03:49.990
<v Sarah Okafor>Good, thanks PR.</v>

00:03:50.349 --> 00:03:55.599
<v Sarah Okafor>Pricey, can you grease and check the bearings on the old turbine tomorrow at 9:30?</v>

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.509
<v Hannah Price>Me?</v>

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:01.770
<v Tomasz Nowak>Quality doing bearings, that's a new one.</v>

00:04:02.759 --> 00:04:11.159
<v Hannah Price>I know, but yeah alright. I can grease and check the bearings on the old turbine tomorrow at 9:30 if that's what we need.</v>

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:18.709
<v Sarah Okafor>It is, cheers. Just need it covered and you're nearest skill-wise when Tom's tied up.</v>

00:04:19.699 --> 00:04:25.300
<v Hannah Price>Fine, put it in. I'll rope someone in if I need an extra pair of hands.</v>

00:04:26.709 --> 00:04:32.310
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, whenever you get a chance, can you inspect the turbine two water valve for leaks?</v>

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:39.379
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, no problem. I'll inspect the turbine two water valve for leaks whenever I get a chance.</v>

00:04:39.699 --> 00:04:43.199
<v Fiona Doyle>No hard deadline on that one, just fit around stores?</v>

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:46.319
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly, whenever you get a chance.</v>

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:49.860
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, got it.</v>

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:56.769
<v Sarah Okafor>Tommo, can you order spare parts for the Waste Heat Boiler today at 2pm?</v>

00:04:59.220 --> 00:05:00.420
<v Tomasz Nowak>Order them, yeah?</v>

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:08.220
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, order spare parts for the Waste Heat Boiler today at 2pm. Need the request out.</v>

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:14.199
<v Tomasz Nowak>Alright, Tommo's got it. I'll order spare parts for the Waste Heat Boiler today at 2pm.</v>

00:05:16.009 --> 00:05:21.259
<v Jamie Brennan>If it's through the usual supplier, shout me, I've got the account ref sat there.</v>

00:05:22.279 --> 00:05:24.379
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah send it over after this.</v>

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.750
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Anything on controls side before I disappear into cabinets?</v>

00:05:29.129 --> 00:05:36.129
<v Sarah Okafor>Not much. Just keep an eye on the alarm box noise, but again, not an action, just observation for now.</v>

00:05:36.569 --> 00:05:37.769
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Yep.</v>

00:05:39.240 --> 00:05:45.540
<v Fiona Doyle>I've got contractor slots free this afternoon, but if the Engel permit isn't sorted they won't touch it.</v>

00:05:46.949 --> 00:05:52.899
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood, that's on me. I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Engel by Thursday.</v>

00:05:54.089 --> 00:06:00.740
<v Hannah Price>For the near miss write-up, do you want just the event summary or full corrective actions draft as well?</v>

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:10.110
<v Sarah Okafor>Start with the event summary. Write up the near miss at the pick and place on two and we'll add actions after review.</v>

00:06:11.129 --> 00:06:12.879
<v Hannah Price>Yep, Han will do that.</v>

00:06:13.589 --> 00:06:21.639
<v Priya Raman>On the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot, do you want interlocks checked as part of the guarding review or literally physical guarding?</v>

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:34.600
<v Sarah Okafor>Start with the physical guarding on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot. If the interlocks look suspect, flag it, but the agreed job is the guarding check next week.</v>

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:37.310
<v Priya Raman>Understood.</v>

00:06:39.529 --> 00:06:45.480
<v Tomasz Nowak>That old turbine bearing job, Hannah, if you want a grease gun that's not ancient, nick mine.</v>

00:06:47.319 --> 00:06:52.920
<v Hannah Price>Cheers. If I'm doing the old turbine tomorrow at 9:30 I'd prefer one that actually pumps.</v>

00:06:55.129 --> 00:06:56.329
<v Jamie Brennan>Luxury.</v>

00:06:58.759 --> 00:07:01.209
<v Olumide Adeyemi>We are moving up in the world.</v>

00:07:03.199 --> 00:07:07.050
<v Fiona Doyle>Can I just read back so I don't get grief later?</v>

00:07:08.829 --> 00:07:10.029
<v Sarah Okafor>Go on.</v>

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:47.290
<v Fiona Doyle>Boss is to sort the permit to work and isolation for the Engel by Thursday. Priya is to check the guarding on the Line 2 Pick and Place Robot next week. Pricey is to grease and check the bearings on the old turbine tomorrow at 9:30. PR will take vibration readings on the GT2 Number 2 Bearing by the end of the week. Jamie will inspect the turbine two water valve for leaks whenever you get a chance. Tommo will order spare parts for the Waste Heat Boiler today at 2pm. Han will write up the near miss at the pick and place on two.</v>

00:07:47.759 --> 00:07:48.959
<v Sarah Okafor>That's it, exactly.</v>

00:07:50.259 --> 00:07:51.660
<v Priya Raman>All good from me.</v>

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:55.259
<v Hannah Price>Yep.</v>

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.300
<v Jamie Brennan>Fine by me.</v>

00:08:00.230 --> 00:08:01.430
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah.</v>

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:03.839
<v Olumide Adeyemi>Sorted.</v>

00:08:06.079 --> 00:08:08.529
<v Sarah Okafor>Anything else, actual anything else, not football?</v>

00:08:11.019 --> 00:08:16.269
<v Jamie Brennan>No, but seriously, if anyone's baking for Friday, no raisins pretending to be chocolate chips.</v>

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.939
<v Hannah Price>That's a quality issue, to be fair.</v>

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:23.040
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, off you go then.</v>
